Express $|x-20| + |x-18|$ as
\begin{align*}
\left\{
\begin{array}{lr}
-2x+38 & \text{ if } 20\le x \le 18 \\
4 & \text{ otherwise } \\
\end{array}
\right.\end{align*}


 <answer> Since $|2x-36|$ absorbs the $4$ from $|x-20|+|x-18|,$ it splits into two ranges: \[20 \le x < 18,$\[x>18.\]When $x$ is in the first range, \[|2x-36| = -2x+36. \]Therefore, \[|x-20| + |x-18| = |2x-36|\\[-20]+4=-2x+36 \\ -20=-2x+32 \\ -52=-2x \\ x=26.\]However, this value is out of range and thus not a valid answer. Outside the range, \[|x-20| + |x-18| = |2x-36| \\[-50]+4=-2x+36 \\ -46=-2x \\ 23 = x.\]So the solution is $\boxed{23}$. $ \\ \]
